Z||000021||Boomtastic||11-05-2000||09:01 PM||||Disgusting - that's all I can say about it. I wouldn't drive that piece of $hit around the block. The welds look like they were done by 4 year olds. Furthermore, it's *not* an '88 Fiero. Not only can you tell by the body (rear bumper pads), but if you look closely at the wheels in the "original" pictures you will see that they are the 1984-85 aluminum 13"x5.5" wheels. 13" wheels _do not_ fit the '88 suspension, as they hit on the brake calipers. $25,000 invested and he's still not done? I think he's smoking the crack pipe. He might have had $25,000 in it with the engine and trans, which are (of course) not included. Otherwise, no freaking way. "1 of a kind"? Naw - I think I'll show him some pictures of mine ...||||reg||13
